is just what i can say  and in the end also interestingly enough  they have some  suggestions on what to do to rectify the  situation  and here is when i don't want to go too  much into the detail but just here the  first one so 80 hours per week should be  considered  max capacity so their demand is to work  80 hours per week and again just to  contrast this with consulting  i'd argue that probably the average in  consulting is around  60 to 65 hours per week and with ups and  downs there will be weeks where you will  also work  more than 80 hours but for sure this is  not the baseline  so it is fair to say that apparently  working in investment banking seems to  be a bit tougher at least at this  specific firm if this is true  then working in consulting of course now  you could also argue that  of course your salary will be a bit  higher and banking especially also in  the long term will be more high it will  be higher in banking than in consulting  and yeah if you just want to read the  rest feel free  so this just some reflections on my end  i'd be super happy to hear from you in  the comments  are you working in banking consulting  does this resonate does this make sense  maybe even some some insiders from gs or  some other firms  let us know what it's really like  whether this is really the case  and if you've never watched this channel  before my name is heinrich  from learning i'm a former mckinsey  consultant usually on my channel i talk  about how to be successful  in the first years of your career i  share tips on slide writing creating  presentations  how to behave in meetings how to  structure your work  so all these things that i learned  during my past work experience  where i try to help you with your work  life as well  so looking forward usually i release  videos every single saturday this was  not a bonus video  so looking forward to that cheers this  is honey from from learning bye bye


